<title>UK: Fuji Bank sets $600 mln step-up perpetual FRN.</title>
<headline>Fuji Bank sets $600 mln step-up perpetual FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers Fuji Bank and Morgan Stanley.  BORROWER   FUJI BANK INTERNATIONAL</p>
<p> AMT    $600 MLN	BASE	*6M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+80 BP    PAY DATE    08.AUG.97</p>
<p> REOFFER    PAR	 ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   0.75</p>
<p> NOTES     *STEPS-UP TO 6M-LIBOR +230 BP ON 08.AUG.02 IF NOT</p>
<p>		CALLED AT PAR. THEN CALLABLE AT PAR ON EACH COUPON</p>
<p>		DATE THEREAFTER.</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMS US/UK/JP/CY</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC   0.25</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
